WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:04.045
She's insane.
How much did she bet on a pig?

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.049
If I'm second place.
I'm out 10 million yen.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:11.469
Well, that doesn't matter.
I can get that amount of money.

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:16.057
The bigger problem is the fact
that she disobeyed me.

00:00:16.641 --> 00:00:21.438
I'll make sure she never fights back.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.773
Congratulations, everyone.

00:00:24.315 --> 00:00:25.984
All ten turns are complete.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:28.945
I will now announce the results.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.780
The winner...

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:33.450
is Mary Saotome,

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.828
with 166 million yen.

00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:39.831
Second place is Nanami Tsubomi,
with 92 million yen.

00:00:39.914 --> 00:00:40.790
Hey, wait!

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.709
Third place is Yumeko Jabami...

00:00:42.792 --> 00:00:44.669
- Hey!
- ...with 74 million yen.

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:47.964
- Fourth place is Jun Kiwatari...
- Wait! You're getting this wrong!

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.718
You're not making a damn bit of sense!

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:54.012
The results are correct.

00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:57.974
Like hell they are!
I've got five Jabami chips!

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:01.728
That's way above 58 million on its own!

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:09.152
Saotome, it's rude to laugh too much.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.825
I didn't think it would work so well!

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:20.413
Part of it was luck, but a lot of it
was thanks to your acting!

00:01:20.497 --> 00:01:22.082
Yeah? Thanks!

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:27.295
You still didn't figure it out?
Do the math.

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:30.215
Two sets of chips
have their values swapped, right?

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:32.383
The chips?

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.761
JABAMI

00:01:34.844 --> 00:01:36.596
God, you're slow at math.

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:39.015
All right, I'll tell you.

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:42.852
Yumeko's and mine are switched.

00:01:43.561 --> 00:01:48.691
Yumeko's chips are worth 5 million yen,
and mine are worth 310 million.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:51.194
See? The math works, right?

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.863
Don't be stupid. You can't just...

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:58.701
It was in the rules, right?
You can write your own amount of debt.

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:04.624
In other words, Yumeko only reported
5 million of her 310 million yen debt.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:11.339
And I have 50 million in debt,
but I reported it as 310 million.

00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:16.553
You said on your application that you took
10 million from a friend, right?

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.931
We did the same thing.

00:02:20.014 --> 00:02:22.308
You weren't the only liar.

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:26.479
An acquaintance of mine
should be getting the money now.

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:29.774
Suzui, message from the student council.

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.071
What the hell is this?

00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:38.199
The rest was simple.

00:02:38.616 --> 00:02:41.327
I received a board
that read "310 million yen,"

00:02:41.411 --> 00:02:43.913
and Yumeko got one
that said "50 million."

00:02:43.955 --> 00:02:46.291
So, we just switched.

00:02:46.916 --> 00:02:48.793
And then, how strange...

00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:54.299
The values of our chips were switched.

